WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.680
<i>We've reached the final set.</i>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.030
<i>To envision beating Nabae-kun as I am now...</i>

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.000
<i>I can think of two ways.</i>

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.410
<i>The first is to strengthen my stroke delivery.</i>

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.410
<i>The other is to add more attack 
patterns when changing the pace.</i>

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.300
<i>If I can pull both of those off...</i>

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.920
<i>I can see a vision of my victory! I think!</i>

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.190
Time.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:34.720
<i>But...</i>

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.650
<i>If I focus on improving my
strokes during this match,</i>

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.780
<i>making more mistakes will be unavoidable.</i>

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.690
<i>And I have to come up with new ways 
to change the pace at the same time.</i>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.690
Bro, hang in there.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>Okay.</i>

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.190
<i>If changing nothing means
I'll lose, I just have to do it!</i>

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.700
<i>I'll make the vision of my victory
a reality here and now!</i>

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.710
Final Set

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.050
Out. 15-love.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.670
<i>His aggressiveness is back.</i>

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.050
<i>He switches gears quickly.</i>

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.320
<i>I somehow hit it back!</i>

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.810
<i>Now, strengthen my delivery!</i>

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.830
Out. 30-love.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.100
<i>Damn!</i>

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.810
<i>But that was a good shot.</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:55.880
Out.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.570
Game: Nabae. 1-0.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.970
<i>I shouldn't consider this recklessness.</i>

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.160
<i>Something unexpected is bound to 
happen from this turn of events.</i>

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.280
<i>If that's the case, the best option is</i>

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.580
<i>to strike him down fast.</i>

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.610
Game: Nabae. 2-0.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.340
Nabae broke serve right off the bat!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.140
He's in a pretty tough spot.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.340
What do you think, Aoi-kun?

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.600
Game: Nabae. 3-0.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.100
<i>If my new strategy for changing the 
pace doesn't work, I'll be cornered.</i>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.770
<i>If I strengthen my delivery 
too much, I make mistakes.</i>

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.060
<i>But this is all I can do right 
now, so I won't hesitate!</i>

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.360
<i>Just keep going!</i>

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.470
<i>Attack with a different pattern:</i>

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.530
<i>a shallow spin!</i>

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:51.850
Love-15.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.090
<i>That just sets him up for his shot!</i>

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.150
<i>If I think on the spot like that, 
my field of vision narrows.</i>

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.130
<i>He's trying to do something?</i>

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.890
<i>Isn't there anything I can do?</i>

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:04.390
<i>I know!</i>

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.140
<i>I'll try Iwasa-kun's</i>

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.490
<i>lob volley!</i>

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.320
Out. Love-30.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.440
<i>It didn't work.</i>

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.400
<i>But other players' strategies 
can give me some ideas.</i>

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.910
<i>Maruo-kun tries new things when he's cornered.</i>

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.730
<i>It's different from how I change my 
play style depending on my opponent.</i>

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.410
<i>He comes up with something 
totally new and evolves it.</i>

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.050
<i>It seems reckless at first,</i>

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.920
<i>but is this what rapid growth on 
the same level as Ike-kun looks like?</i>

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.250
Yes!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.270
Game: Maruo. 3-1.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.380
Nabae leads.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.430
<i>It looks like changing his attitude brought 
him closer to being in the zone.</i>

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.810
Game: Maruo. 4-2.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.930
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.930
Nabae leads.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.860
It's turned into a battle to 
hold serve for both of them.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.440
Bro is getting into the swing of things!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.550
Love-15.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.690
<i>I feel like I'm close to being in the zone again.</i>

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.710
<i>No, no!</i>

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>I blew it before because 
I thought about this too much!</i>

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.660
<i>I won't think about the zone anymore!</i>

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.710
<i>Next is...</i>

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.960
<i>Trying to volley again?</i>

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.470
<i>He stopped?!</i>

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.810
Love-30.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.990
Yes!

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.640
<i>The strategy I lost to in that match 
with Takuma-san gave me a clue!</i>

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.230
<i>I just have to keep using the data I have</i>

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.320
<i>to change the pace however I can 
and deliver it with strong strokes.</i>

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.500
<i>I also feel like I'm close to the zone, 
but I won't think about that now!</i>

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.250
<i>This is his first chance at 
a break since the first set.</i>

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.980
<i>It isn't just difficult to read his pattern.</i>

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:05.510
<i>His occasional strong shots increase 
the variety in the tempo of his rallies.</i>

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.260
<i>He tries neither to suppress 
his emotions nor to release them,</i>

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.360
<i>but to control them.</i>

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:16.020
<i>It's an unstable method, but 
when it works, it's intimidating.</i>

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.020
<i>I'm leading by one break.</i>

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.530
<i>The real fight begins here!</i>

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.930
15-30.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.610
Unlucky break for Maruo!

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.390
<i>That was a good serve. I couldn't 
do anything about that one.</i>

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.540
30-all.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.850
An ace!

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:40.360
That's Nabae for you. He's already caught up!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.380
<i>Couldn't do anything about that one, either.</i>

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.340
<i>I returned it! But it's weak, so he'll go for it!</i>

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:55.890
<i>I'll use that weak hit to my advantage and 
force it down the line with my hardest swing!</i>

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.640
<i>He usually hits down the line 
after this many good shots.</i>

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:02.650
<i>No...</i>

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.900
30-40.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.320
Yes!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.400
Nice one!

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.830
<i>If Nabae-kun's going to use 
previous data to predict my moves,</i>

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.460
<i>I'll come up with new 
patterns to change the pace.</i>

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>And when Nabae-kun starts to hesitate, 
I'll hit a stronger stroke.</i>

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.420
<i>I'll watch him carefully so I can 
alter my moves at the last second.</i>

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.850
<i>This is it!</i>

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.340
<i>This is my vision of how I'll win!</i>

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.200
<i>But that's insanely difficult to pull off!</i>

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.060
<i>A deep, but strong, sharply-angled spin!</i>

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:47.680
<i>Move up early!</i>

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.190
<i>He read me!</i>

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:57.760
<i>The odds aren't good, but I'll 
follow the spin with a strong flat!</i>

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.990
Game: Maruo. 4-3.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.070
Nabae leads.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.270
Yeah!

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.650
Maruo broke serve this time!

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.640
He's tough!

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.720
He's seriously strong!

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.230
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.230
He broke the serve that Nabae
was trying to hold at any cost!

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:24.900
<i>There was a lot of speculation 
about who would be able to</i>

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.420
<i>break Nabae-kun's chokehold,</i>

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:30.760
<i>but what an unexpected candidate.</i>

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.970
<i>It's only one game, but I was able to 
make the vision of my win a reality!</i>

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:40.090
<i>But I now know how difficult that is to do.</i>

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:44.230
<i>Strategically, I need both the creativity 
to come up with new patterns</i>

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.170
<i>and the execution to win points with it.</i>

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.690
<i>And emotionally, I need to be composed 
and driven at the same time.</i>

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.670
<i>Both strategically and emotionally,</i>

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.790
<i>I need to balance all the factors 
that don't coexist easily</i>

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.990
<i>in order to realize my vision of victory.</i>

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:03.230
<i>Now that it's close, I want to get rid of 
my emotions without giving up a point.</i>

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.270
<i>With the purest determination possible,</i>

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:10.730
<i>I have to calmly observe both myself and 
my opponent to accurately determine</i>

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.690
<i>the best way to go about this battle.</i>

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:20.400
Time.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.920
15-love.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.160
All right!

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.150
Game: Maruo. 4-all.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.430
Bro! You finally came back from a 3-0 deficit!

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:44.180
I can't believe an unseeded player
is giving Nabae so much trouble.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.960
<i>Maruo-kun is overreaching himself.</i>

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.630
15-love.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.690
<i>This style could definitely become a threat.</i>

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.840
<i>But if I want to win today, 
I just have to reduce risk factors.</i>

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:03.490
<i>It's too risky to go after both 
the flat and the spin shots.</i>

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.940
<i>Is it safest to go after just the spins?</i>

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:07.460
15-all.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:09.710
Out.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.550
30-15.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:14.400
<i>I can't help making mistakes 
when visualizing a win as I play.</i>

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.930
<i>It may look like just a 
mistake to everyone else,</i>

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.970
<i>but it's most likely the best I can do.</i>

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.740
<i>I couldn't even make a dent last time,</i>

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:26.010
<i>but now I'm playing toe-to-toe against 
the All-Japan champion in the final set,</i>

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:27.390
<i>so there's no mistake.</i>

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.650
<i>I studied in Florida,</i>

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.400
<i>fortified my serve,</i>

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.400
<i>and trained my muscles.</i>

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:37.150
<i>I'm hitting this shot with nothing on my mind</i>

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.270
<i>except changing the pace!</i>

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.410
30-all.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.040
That's amazing!

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:44.910
I never imagined Maruo getting this far!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.560
40-30.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.160
Based solely on his spirit,
I'd go with Maruo-kun, but...

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.260
<i>He moved up!</i>

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.660
Game: Nabae. 5-4.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:56.500
Final set.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.400
This is what I'm talking about!

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.510
Even if it's a difficult volley, he has the 
stability to score while keeping his cool.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.930
His composure and technique 
in situations like this

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.680
are what allow him to remain the king.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.690
<i>I can't lose the next game.</i>

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:12.810
Nabae, this is it!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.060
You can do it, Maruo!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.390
Game: Maruo. 5-all.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:25.330
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.520
They're both battling to hold serve.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:24.200
But Maruo is aware of the risks he's taking.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.330
That makes it easier for him to miss.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.980
Out. Game: Nabae. 6-5.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:30.710
Final set.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.180
You have to hold this next one, Bro!

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.710
If he breaks serve, Nabae-kun wins, huh?

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.720
<i>Realizing my vision of winning 
over and over isn't that easy.</i>

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.150
<i>And if this match gets drawn out,</i>

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.840
<i>I'm aware that I'll be the one suffering.</i>

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:48.310
<i>The final set will continue on until 
someone gets a two-game lead.</i>

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.230
<i>So I need to try to settle it 
quickly and decisively!</i>

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.990
<i>Hold serve here, and break serve next!</i>

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:56.730
<i>Then hold serve in the end, and win!</i>

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.990
<i>I'm prepared for a long match.</i>

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.990
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.210
<i>But I'll end it here.</i>

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:04.990
Time.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.500
<i>I need a minimum of three games to win.</i>

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.230
<i>No matter what strategy Nabae-kun uses,</i>

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:23.020
<i>I'll fight back with a vision 
of sending it back to win.</i>

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.030
<i>I need to go all-out,</i>

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.220
<i>but make sure this first serve goes in!</i>

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.650
<i>His serves are getting closer to the edge.</i>

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.520
<i>If he's going to be this risky,</i>

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.810
<i>I'll emphasize defense.</i>

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.950
Out. Love-15.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.530
<i>This is good enough for now.</i>

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:46.280
<i>Nabae-kun is starting to 
play a little defensively.</i>

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:49.990
<i>But if I let that beat me, 
I can't call this my winning vision.</i>

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.960
<i>Be prepared to make some mistakes</i>

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.910
<i>to pull off the win I envisioned!</i>

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.750
<i>I'm ready for this!</i>

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.390
<i>I'll go after him early with a stronger stroke!</i>

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.130
<i>Now surprise him!</i>

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.140
<i>A sudden lob after he had the upper hand?</i>

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.640
<i>He isn't moving up.</i>

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:16.390
<i>Now he moves up?</i>

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.880
<i>What'll he do?</i>

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.400
<i>A drive volley?!</i>

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.080
Yes!

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.160
15-all.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:32.090
Miyagawa's drive volleys 
gave Bro a beating, after all.

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:35.590
His irregular combination of shots 
before that is what was impressive.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.170
It's a lot like Natsu.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.740
<i>It was dangerous since it 
barely went over the net,</i>

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.410
<i>but I was able to calmly pull 
off what I set out to do!</i>

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.170
<i>I can do this! I can win!</i>

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:49.530
<i>If I can beat Nabae-kun, they'll 
surely accept my decision to go pro.</i>

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.680
<i>I can do what I love 
without making them worry!</i>

00:13:56.740 --> 00:14:00.690
<i>If his shots are this good, there's only 
so much I can do by playing defensively.</i>

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.410
Bro's really pushing him!

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:03.940
No, not exactly.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.830
<i>Keep my defense airtight,</i>

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:08.080
<i>and when I attack, go for it in one shot!</i>

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.700
<i>A drop shot?!</i>

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.300
15-30.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.360
Who can land a drop shot at a time like this?!

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.960
How is he so calm?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.430
<i>Not yet...</i>

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.220
15-40.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.220
Nabae's got match point.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:34.920
All right!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.970
Okay! Match point!

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.230
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.960
<i>Nabae-kun's got match point.</i>

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.890
<i>If he wins the next point, I'll lose.</i>

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.710
<i>Then...</i>

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.410
<i>I'll make this pressure my weapon!</i>

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.420
<i>The vision of my win is right there!</i>

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:34.780
Out.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.050
Game, set, and match.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.290
Winner: Nabae.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.790
Score: 4-6, 6-2, 7-5.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.820
It's finally over!

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.840
Nabae's advancing to the final!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.570
No less from Nabae.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:14.320
Nabae Yu
Maruo Eiichiro

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.170
He pulls it off when it counts.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.320
No, he was totally in danger this time.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.530
<i>I did everything I needed to.</i>

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.900
<i>And I pulled off everything I could.</i>

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.350
<i>I got all the way to the final set,</i>

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.870
<i>but a loss is a loss.</i>

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.000
<i>I still can't beat Nabae-kun.</i>

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.240
Making the top four in Kanto isn't too shabby.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:37.850
Coach Aoi.

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:41.740
More like this was the best I could do.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.880
I have to become stronger.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:48.720
Oh, but I'm glad I was able to test out 
a bunch of things thanks to you.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.870
And now I have a better idea of 
what I have to do in the future.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.300
That's good.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:58.370
By the way, there's someone 
I wanted to introduce you to.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.510
Hey, Maruo-kun, that was a great match.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:02.870
I was moved.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:05.720
Huh? Th-Thank you very much.

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:08.880
He's from the company that makes your racket.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:13.320
The way you use both mind and body 
to the fullest to play tennis

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:16.640
is not only new, but it's also fascinating!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.890
Oh...

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:23.380
Which is why we were hoping 
you would use our new racket.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.390
What do you think?

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.850
<i>What? Does that mean...</i>

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:27.760
That's right.

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:31.520
We'd like you to help us come up with
future racket designs as a tester.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.780
<i>I get to be a racket tester</i>

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.870
<i>just like Araya-kun and Nabae-kun?</i>

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.700
<i>This is a huge deal, isn't it?</i>

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.890
Hello?

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.420
Oh, Kageyama.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.090
Hey, Ei-chan.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.330
How'd it go today?

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.840
What? You lost? I see...

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:00.930
But it's amazing that you got all 
the way to Kanto's top four!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.870
Yeah. But it's not enough.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.870
I'm going to stay and watch tomorrow's final.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.090
<i>Okay. Don't get down on yourself!</i>

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:09.920
Yeah. Thanks.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:14.940
<i>The Kanto Junior final round will now begin.</i>

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:18.450
The final ended up being Araya versus Nabae.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:23.620
Yeah. I wonder how Araya-kun 
plans to beat Nabae-kun.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.460
Probably with his speed and power.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.460
Yeah!

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.460
15-love.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:37.170
But Bro, the next time you play 
against Nabae, I think you'll win.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:41.210
Well, I have to, or I won't be able 
to win the All-Japan Junior.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.960
Last year, you lost bigtime against Nabae.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.800
"Bigtime"? Come on...

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:49.290
But it's true that I lost 6-2, 6-1 in straight sets.

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:53.840
And this year, you fought him toe-to-toe
all the way to the final set.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:56.940
You've improved at a phenomenal speed.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:04.930
<i>That's right. When I first started,
I couldn't even keep up during warm-ups.</i>

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:08.820
Can't do it.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.540
Coach! He passed out!

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.890
<i>I lost my first match, but it was fun.</i>

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.210
<i>It made me like tennis even more.</i>

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:23.570
<i>As I won more, I got to play 
against stronger opponents.</i>

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:26.470
<i>I learned a lot from everyone.</i>

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.980
<i>It's been two and a half years 
since I started tennis...</i>

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.480
Nabae Yu
Araya Hiroshi

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.810
Game, set, and match. Winner: Takasaki.

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:41.240
I did it! I did it!

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.240
Score: 6-2, 6-2.

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.150
Nat-chan won.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:47.640
She probably didn't lose a single 
set this year and won outright.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.000
That's amazing.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.500
<i>Because Nat-chan was there for me...</i>

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.040
I want to go pro.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:59.550
I'm sure Ei-chan will play a big role.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:03.380
That means this is our starting line.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.510
Yeah.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:06.280
Then...

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:09.770
What would you want me to say?

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:14.940
Seeing you work hard has always 
made me want to work hard, too.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:18.480
Even when I've got it rough, 
I can tell myself to overcome it.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:23.160
So when you win, I'm as happy as if I had won,

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.990
and that always gives me strength!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:30.270
Game, set, and match. Winner: Araya.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.360
All right!

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:34.260
Score: 4-6, 7-5, 7-5.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.220
What?! Nabae-kun lost?

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.640
It didn't look like Nabae was 
playing the way he usually does.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:41.760
Yeah, Araya-kun was good, but Nabae-kun 
made a lot of mistakes today.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:46.670
You tried to play a power game against me.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:48.650
What were you thinking?

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:58.770
<i>I see.</i>

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.700
<i>Maybe Nabae-kun was thinking 
more about the future</i>

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.490
<i>while playing this final match today.</i>

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.670
<i>Alex made it into the top 
500 in the world ranking.</i>

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:25.250
Yes!

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.180
Game: Alex. 3-0.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.670
Yeah, Alex! Good show!

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:32.130
Alex'll probably have a straight-set win.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:34.680
He might just keep this up
and win the whole thing.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:36.560
<i>Not yet...</i>

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:40.190
<i>I'm going to go even further.</i>

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:43.190
You can do it, Alex.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:48.200
<i>Takuma-san won his third pro 
tournament match recently.</i>

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.590
That'll bring your rank up even higher.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.120
I'm just getting started.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.210
I have to go even higher.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:07.470
<i>Ike-kun played against the world's 
number one player in a Grand Slam.</i>

00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:18.960
You completely defeated me today.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.100
I'll make our next match even better.

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:26.330
<i>Among all these incredible people,</i>

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:27.930
<i>I wonder how far I can go.</i>

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:30.500
Ei-chan!

00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:34.060
Bro!

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:36.090
Hurry up, Eiichiro!

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:40.180
Let's go!

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:42.530
Yeah!

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:50.450
<i>I'll take it one step at a time.</i>

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:52.590
<i>I'll go even further,</i>

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:54.940
<i>by believing in myself.</i>

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
